tweets.full_text:
The reason I do fewer conferences lately is that I just hate flying. No anxiety or fear but just sheer hatred of the logistics and time.

With my annual U.S.-Egypt route (which I also dislike the logistics of, and it eats into my tolerance), every other trip is hard to agree to.

@VladTheInflator I have flown private, but I usually fly business class.

Private gets harder when you go international.

@Principoshi It's where most of my family and friends are.

@VladTheInflator @grok explain why private jets get harder when you go overseas.

@grok @VladTheInflator Thanks.

@grok @VladTheInflator https://t.co/yrcrVG07OY

@JorgeFranc97ko Indeed.

@EricBalchunas From 2021-2024 I felt that way.

After that I became old or rich or something. Mainly it was a work-life balance view.

I hate travel and will do it far less often now. I mostly do it for friends.

I used to joke with my colleagues. I drove an old Hyundai and I paid more than its value per flight.

In recent years I’m in the arc of avoiding suffering. I went previously went through suffering, and now I’m like “nope”.

But now, I can throw any amount of money at a flight, or have it covered at many conferences. But it’s not the money. It’s the logistics. Putting yourself into drive-airport-airline-control mayhem you have no say over.

